<title>USA: American Intl Pete buys Kazakh stake.</title>
<headline>American Intl Pete buys Kazakh stake.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Independent energy company American International Petroleum Corp said on Wednesday that it would pay MED Shipping and Trading Ltd, a consortium of western and Kazakh businessmen, 1.5 million of its own shares to purchase a 70 percent stake in a 4.7 million acre offshore oil license in Kazahkstan.</p>
<p>The shares must be held in trust and may not be sold until the American stock price reaches $5.00, the company said.</p>
